From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Load window: preview renders of each park, framed on its
 built area

"openrct2 screenshot <file> <image> preview <width> <height>" renders a
park at its saved rotation, framed on the area it is built on: the tiles
with two or more elements besides the surface, weighted by that count
squared and trimmed by 1% of the weight on each side, with every element's
height counted. It uses the closest zoom level that fits, and past the
widest level renders larger and reduces by a whole factor, keeping each
block's most common colour. The void is transparent.

The Load window renders every file it shows without such a picture, one
at a time in the background, by running its own executable with that
command (hidden, at low priority, output discarded). Renders are kept in
the cache folder's "previews" folder, named from the file's path, size and
modification time; a file that fails leaves an empty ".none" file so it is
not tried again. Tiles and the preview pane use the render instead of the
file's embedded screenshot, which saves older than the embedded previews
and RCT2 saves lack; the pane leaves out the park summary when the file
has none.
